course: dictionary
lesson: 2136
title: Coolness and its meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Coolness is a noun, a thing you can notice or feel. It has more than one meaning, so the words around it show you which one is meant.
explain: «Dock leaves on nettle stings help mostly because rubbing and coolness soothe; they are not a strong chemical cure.» Here coolness is a gentle cold feeling. The clue is soothe, which means to calm pain or make it easier.
explain: Coolness can also mean calm when things are tense, as in coolness under pressure. It can mean unfriendliness, as in a coolness between them. Ask yourself: is this about temperature, feelings, or people? Then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Coolness means being a little cold in a pleasant way, such as the coolness of the evening on a hot day.
fact: Coolness means being calm and not getting nervous or excited, such as coolness under pressure.
fact: Coolness can mean being unfriendly, as in a coolness between them, which shows a quarrel or distance.
fact: Coolness can also mean being fashionable or impressive.
fact: In «Dock leaves on nettle stings help mostly because rubbing and coolness soothe», coolness means a gentle cold that soothes, not a strong medicine.
exercise: «Dock leaves on nettle stings help mostly because rubbing and coolness soothe.» What does coolness mean here? | A strong chemical medicine | A loud noise made by the leaves | *A gentle cold feeling that calms the sting | Being unfriendly to the nettle
exercise: «She kept her coolness under pressure when the match was tied.» What does coolness mean here? | Being a little cold in a pleasant way | Being fashionable | Being unfriendly | *Staying calm and not getting nervous
exercise: Which phrase suggests that two friends are not getting on well? | *a coolness between them | the coolness of the evening | coolness under pressure
test: Which meaning fits «the coolness of the evening» after a hot day? | *A pleasant little cold | Staying calm under stress | Being unfriendly | Being fashionable
test: In the nettle sentence, why do dock leaves help? | *Rubbing and coolness soothe the sting | They make the nettle disappear | They are a strong chemical cure | They are very fashionable
exam: Read «Her coolness under pressure helped the team win.» What does coolness mean? | Being unfriendly | A pleasant little cold | Being fashionable | *Staying calm and not getting nervous
